counterfactuals.output:
A method for manufacturing a three-dimensional metal mold, comprising:

1. providing a build platform and metal powder suitable for selective laser sintering or selective laser melting;

2. forming a powder layer of the metal powder over the build platform;

3. selectively irradiating the powder layer with an energy beam according to slice data derived from three-dimensional mold data, thereby sintering or melting selected regions of the powder layer to form a solidified metal layer;

4. lowering the build platform by a predetermined layer thickness and repeating the powder-layer forming and selective irradiation steps to integrally build the metal mold layer by layer;

5. during said layer-by-layer building, leaving predetermined regions unsintered or unmelted so as to define an internal flow path configured to convey a cooling medium, the internal flow path extending along a prescribed three-dimensional contour; and

6. forming, on a molding surface or a surface adjacent thereto, a concave-convex portion having a contour shape corresponding to the prescribed three-dimensional contour of the internal flow path,

wherein the internal flow path and the concave-convex portion are formed integrally with the metal mold by the repeated powder-layer formation and selective sintering or melting, and wherein the concave-convex portion and the internal flow path have substantially the same contour shape when viewed in a direction normal to the molding surface.

The method may further comprise removing unsintered or unmelted powder from the internal flow path through at least one inlet or outlet, heat-treating the built metal mold, machining a reference surface, and polishing or texturing the concave-convex portion while retaining its contour correspondence with the internal flow path.
